sentences.text:
MISC. No.78217 of 2025(2) dt.03-12-2025 period of six weeks from the receipt of this order, on furnishing bail bond of Rs. 10,000/- (Ten Thousand)
with two sureties of the like amount each in connection with aforesaid P.S. Case to the satisfaction of learned CJM, Supaul, subject to the conditions as laid down under Section 482(2) of the BNSS as also subject to the following conditions:-
(i) one of the bailors should be the family member/relative of the petitioners who shall provide official document to show his/her bona fide;
(ii) the petitioners shall appear on each and every date before the Trial Court and failure to do so for two consecutive dates without plausible reason will entail cancellation of their bail bond by the Trial Court itself;
(iii) the petitioners shall co-operate in the investigation and make themselves available to the police as and when required;

